theorem one-equation-and-a-constant
  note        The equation s = 1 is read as the order s ≥ 1 by a weakening
              row, and s ≥ 0 follows from that one line with a constant to
              spare, 1 > 0, which the step takes without writing it.
  let s ∈ ℝ                                                           (H1)
  assume s = 1                                                        (H2)
  then s ≥ 0

1.  s ≥ 1
    inequalities
      s = 1            H2
      s ≥ 1            weakening

2.  s ≥ 0
    inequalities, from 1
